;; holder-registry.edn — who is accountable for each owning record, NOW.
;;
;; Why this file exists (Joe, 2026-08-31): all 80 contract declarations carried
;; `holder: claude-15`. When that session was poisoned, responsibility for the entire
;; formal spine went with it — one session held the contract, the gate and the queue.
;; Nothing GATED on the field (contract_lint only passes it through), so nothing broke
;; mechanically; what was lost was the answer to "who is accountable".
;;
;; The fix is indirection, not renaming. Holes.lean now says `holder: by-record`, so a
;; declaration's holder is resolved through its DURABLE `owner` record and this table.
;; Reassignment is one line here, not 77 edits in Lean.
;;
;; :holder must be a live agent on the Agency roster, or :unassigned (loud, not silent —
;; checks/holder_check.clj exits 1 on any unassigned or dead holder, per I_absent_is_loud).
;; Declaration counts are deliberately absent. They duplicated the generated contract,
;; were never consumed, and drifted from 80 to 100 declarations while dated today.
{:as-of "2026-08-31"
 :resolves "contract declaration -> its `owner` record -> the holder below"
 :checked-by "futon2/checks/holder_check.clj"
 :records
